<Prose title="About Best Home Theater Review: Who We Are and How We Work" description="Best Home Theater Review is an independent home theater buying guide with its own testing lab. Recommendations show their working, and rankings are never sold." h1="About Best Home Theater Review" path="/about/" pageType="AboutPage" intro="An independent buying guide for people building a home theater, from a first soundbar to a dedicated room.">
  <h2>What We Do</h2>
  <p>Most home theater "best of" lists repeat the marketing copy. We start from the spec sheet and do the maths: how far a projector must sit from your screen, how many speakers a receiver can actually power at once, how much amplifier headroom a speaker's sensitivity demands, and what all of that costs.</p>
  <p>Today we track <strong>{products.length} products</strong> from <strong>{brands.length} brands</strong> across <strong>{articles.length} in-depth guides</strong>, and we update them as new models arrive and old ones are discontinued.</p>
  <h2>How We're Different</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>We show our working.</strong> Every recommendation explains the spec that matters and the calculation behind it.</li>
    <li><strong>Room first, product second.</strong> The right receiver, sub or projector depends on your room size, seating distance and light, so our picks say who each one suits.</li>
    <li><strong>We tell you when to skip it.</strong> Every product page has a "skip it if" line, and our brand reviews say where each brand falls short.</li>
    <li><strong>No paid placements.</strong> Brands cannot pay to be included or ranked. See our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Who Writes the Guides</h2>
  <p>Our guides and reviews are written by <a href={AUTHOR.url}>{AUTHOR.name}</a>, a software engineer with a background in embedded systems and digital signal processing (previously at Apple and Tesla; University of Waterloo Computer Science).</p>
  <h2>Our Lab</h2>
  <p>We have our own testing lab in {LAB.location}. Products that have been through it carry a <strong>Lab tested</strong> badge, with the test date, method and results on their gear page.</p>
  <h2>How We Score</h2>
  <p>Every product gets a BHTR Score out of 100. Our <a href="/how-we-test/">methodology page</a> explains exactly what goes into it and, just as importantly, what we don't claim.</p>
  <h2>How We Make Money</h2>
  <p>We earn a commission when you buy through some of our links, mainly Amazon, at no extra cost to you. Commissions never decide rankings. Full details are on our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Spotted an error, or want us to cover a product? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or use our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. We correct factual errors quickly and note material updates on the page.</p>
</Prose>
